    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^2-y^2=a^2$.\n\nSquare both expressions and subtract, using $\\sec^2\\theta-\\tan^2\\theta=1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-y^2&=(a\\sec\\theta)^2-(a\\tan\\theta)^2\\\\x^2-y^2&=a^2(\\sec^2\\theta-\\tan^2\\theta)\\\\x^2-y^2&=a^2.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $\\sec^2\\theta-\\tan^2\\theta=1$.",
